---
import SystemPage from '../../components/v2/SystemPage.astro';
import { imagery } from '../../content/imagery';

const v2 = imagery.v2;
---

<SystemPage
	title="Storm damage roofing"
	heroEyebrow="Residential · storm damage"
	heroHeading="Storm damage?<br />We handle the whole roof."
	heroLede="Hail, wind, tree fall, water intrusion. Free inspection, full damage documentation, direct work with your insurance adjuster. You pay your deductible. We do the rest."
	heroPhoto={v2.pageHeros.stormDamage}
	heroCta={{ label: 'Storm damage inspection', href: '/free-inspection' }}
	bleedPhoto={v2.bleeds.storm}
	bleedHeading="Hail. Wind. Tree fall.<br />We handle the whole job."
	overview={{
		eyebrow: 'What we do on a storm claim',
		heading: 'Inspection. Documentation. Adjuster meeting. Install.',
		body: "Heritage handles storm damage as an end-to-end job: free roof inspection within 24–48 hours of your call, full photo and video documentation of damage, direct meeting with your insurance adjuster on-site, supplement requests when the initial estimate undervalues scope, and the install once the claim is approved. You handle your deductible. We handle everything else."
	}}
	keyPoints={[
		{
			heading: 'How insurance claims actually work.',
			body: "You report damage to your insurer. They send an adjuster. The adjuster writes a scope and a number. Heritage meets the adjuster on-site, walks the roof together, and makes sure the scope is complete. If the carrier's number is short, we file a supplement with the documentation. The carrier issues payment minus your deductible. We do the work.",
			bullets: ['Free inspection within 24–48 hours', 'On-site adjuster meeting', 'Photo + video documentation', 'Supplement requests when needed'],
			photo: v2.serviceTiles.storm,
			photoSide: 'left',
		},
		{
			heading: 'What gets covered.',
			body: "Hail damage to shingles (granule loss, fractures, exposed mat). Wind damage (lifted, missing, or torn shingles). Tree fall (puncture, structural). Water intrusion from any of the above. Insurance covers the roof replacement; coverage for related items (interior ceiling damage, gutters, fence) depends on your policy.",
			bullets: ['Hail damage (granule loss, mat exposure)', 'Wind damage (missing, lifted, torn shingles)', 'Tree fall + impact', 'Water intrusion + ceiling damage'],
			photo: v2.bleeds.workmanship,
			photoSide: 'right',
		},
	]}
	stats={[
		{ value: '24–48', label: 'Hours to first inspection' },
		{ value: '$0', label: 'Out-of-pocket beyond deductible' },
		{ value: '100%', label: 'Adjuster on-site for documented claims' },
		{ value: '7 days', label: 'Typical claim → install · Heritage average' },
	]}
	projectPhotos={[v2.projects[0], v2.projects[1], v2.projects[6], v2.projects[7]]}
	projectCaptions={['Hail damage replacement, Tyler', 'Wind damage claim, Longview', 'Tree fall + roof rebuild, Marshall', 'Insurance install, Kilgore']}
	faq={[
		{ q: "Will my premium go up?", a: '<p>In Texas, premiums don\'t go up on a single weather-related claim filed properly. (General guidance — your specific carrier and policy govern. We\'re not insurance professionals; talk to your agent on this.)</p>' },
		{ q: "Do I pay anything upfront?", a: '<p>Your deductible is what you pay out of pocket. Some carriers send the deductible directly to the contractor; some send it to you. Heritage works with both arrangements. Anything beyond your deductible is between Heritage and the carrier.</p>' },
		{ q: "How long does the whole process take?", a: '<p>Free inspection: 24–48 hours from your call. Adjuster meeting: typically within a week of your claim being filed. Approval: 1–2 weeks after the adjuster visit. Install: same week as approval, weather permitting. Most full claims close inside 30 days.</p>' },
		{ q: "What if my claim is denied?", a: '<p>If the adjuster sees no covered damage, we write up our findings independently — sometimes that re-opens the claim with a different adjuster. If the damage is real but the carrier disagrees on scope, we file a supplement. If there\'s genuinely no covered damage, we tell you that and you don\'t pay us anything.</p>' },
		{ q: "Do you handle the paperwork?", a: '<p>Yes. We handle the adjuster meeting, the scope discussion, supplement requests with photo evidence, and most of the back-and-forth. You sign the documents and stay informed; we do the work.</p>' },
		{ q: "What about emergency tarping?", a: '<p>Available 24/7. If your roof is actively leaking, we tarp first to stop the water, then handle the inspection and claim process during business hours.</p>' },
	]}
	ctaHeading="Storm damage?<br />Inspection in 24 hours."
	ctaLede="Free inspection. We handle the adjuster, the scope, and the install."
	ctaPhoto={v2.pageHeros.stormDamage}
	ctaPrimary={{ label: 'Storm damage inspection', href: '/free-inspection' }}
	promises={['Insurance accepted · all carriers', '24/7 emergency tarp', 'Adjuster on-site · documented claims']}
/>
